# Copy to `.env` for local development. Do not put production values here —
# `.env` is gitignored, this template is not.

# Postgres. Read by both the Prisma CLI (via prisma.config.ts) and the app —
# unlike Turso, there is no separate variable for either side. A quick local
# instance:
#
#   docker run -d -p 5432:5432 -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres postgres
#
# then `pnpm db:migrate` to apply the schema to it.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/ttgamba"

# Optional. Redis for query caching — see lib/db.ts for which models are cached
# and, more importantly, which deliberately are not.
#
# Left empty, caching is off and nothing tries to connect: development needs no
# Redis running. Redis being unreachable in production is also survivable, by
# design — cache errors are reported and never thrown, so queries fall through
# to the database. Dragonfly speaks the same protocol, so this points there
# just as well as at real Redis.
#
#   REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"
REDIS_URL=""
